				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1085
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέλειμμαι τῶν ἐν Ἕλλησιν νόμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1246
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>to be defeated</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.62.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπό τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.224
				</span></i>
			 (Antip.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λείπεσθαι ἐν [τῇ
				ἀγορανομίᾳ</span>], Lat. <i>repulsam ferre</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Mar.</u>
				5
			</span></i>, etc.: abs., in part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρας λελειμμένους</span>
			<i>inferior</i> men, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				37
			</span></i>; also, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λειπόμενοι</span>”
